msgid "Design goal"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/backend/js.md:5
msgid "The specification describes a second realization path: MoonBit code compiled to JavaScript that passes typed array buffers to a Node.js addon, which calls the same C runtime as the native backend. `backend/js` reserves the package for that path and fixes its identity, so that the rest of the module can already name the JavaScript target in policies, capability tables and submissions."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/backend/js.md:11
#: manual/design/backend/native.md:15
#: manual/design/core.md:11
#: manual/design/plan.md:11
#: manual/design/shared.md:11
#: manual/design/workflow.md:12
msgid "Mathematical background"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/backend/js.md:13
msgid "The package computes nothing. The only structure it takes part in is the backend sum type"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/backend/js.md:20
msgid "with each backend package providing the constant $\\texttt{backend\\_target} \\in B$ that names it. For the JavaScript package this constant is $\\mathrm{JavaScript}$, and the v1 policy subset $P_1$ described on the [shared design](../shared.md) page excludes it, so every policy or submission that names this backend is rejected before reaching any runtime."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/backend/js.md:26
#: manual/design/backend/native.md:103
#: manual/design/core.md:35
#: manual/design/plan.md:35
#: manual/design/shared.md:62
