msgid "Design decisions"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/backend/js.md:28
msgid "A package before a backend"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/backend/js.md:30
msgid "Declaring the package now keeps the module layout of the specification (`backend/native` and `backend/js` side by side) and lets code depend on `@js.backend_target()` rather than on a constructor of `shared`. When the backend is implemented, its foreign declarations and wrappers go here without a new import path."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/backend/js.md:36
msgid "No foreign declarations yet"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/backend/js.md:38
msgid "The addon in `js/` exports only `runtimeName` and does not link the C runtime, so there is nothing to declare. Declaring functions with no implementation would compile but fail at run time, which is worse than not offering them."
msgstr ""

